course: dictionary
lesson: 1826
title: Coarse: rough, big, or rude
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the context tells you which one to use. «Shaving does not change how thick, dark or fast hair grows; cut hair just has a blunt tip that feels coarser.» Coarser here means rougher to touch, because the sentence is about how hair feels.
explain: Look at the words around coarse. Coarse sand, coarse salt and coarsely chopped onion are about size and texture: they are made of big pieces or feel rough. Coarse jokes and coarse language are about manners: they are rude or crude.
explain: Ask yourself: what does the rest of the sentence describe? If it describes how something feels or looks, coarse means rough. If it describes how someone talks or acts, coarse means rude. Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it makes sense.
fact: Coarse means rough and thick to touch, not smooth or fine.
fact: Coarse can also mean made of big pieces or grains, as in «coarse salt».
fact: Coarse can mean rude, crude or vulgar, as in «coarse jokes».
fact: In UK fishing, «coarse fishing» means fishing for freshwater fish other than salmon and trout.
fact: Coarser is the comparison form, and coarsest is the strongest form.
exercise: Mia rubs her hand across the coarse sandpaper. What does coarse mean here? | Shiny and bright | Cold and wet | Soft and silky | *Rough and not smooth
exercise: The cook says, «Use coarse salt, not fine salt.» What does coarse describe? | *Big grains, not fine ones | Wet and sticky | Made of gold | Very expensive
exercise: «Shaving does not change how thick, dark or fast hair grows; cut hair just has a blunt tip that feels coarser.» What does coarser mean here? | *Rougher to touch | Faster to grow | Thicker in length | Darker in colour
test: In a story, a man makes coarse jokes at dinner. What does coarse mean? | *Rude and vulgar | Made of tiny grains | Very funny and kind | Quiet and shy
test: Anglers in the UK go coarse fishing. What do they catch? | *Freshwater fish other than salmon and trout | Sea fish only | Fish kept in tanks at home | Only salmon
exam: The recipe says «coarsely chopped onion». Which meaning of coarse fits best? | *Big pieces, not fine | Smooth and shiny | Rude and crude | Very quick
